# ── Facts for writing the post ──────────────────────────────
# Raw material, not copy. Shown on /studio/downloads/ so the post can be
# written on a phone without switching back to a laptop to look something
# up. Every line here is checked against the site or src/_data — a line
# starting "ASK:" is a gap only Terry or Dalton can fill.
#
# Keep this list true. It is the thing someone will trust at 6am.
facts:
  - group: "The people — lead with this"
    items:
      - "Terry Booker and Dalton Watkins, business partners, are the two names on the door."
      - "This post gets shared by friends and family first. They recognise a name long before an address, so open on the people, not the premises."
      - "ASK: how long has each of them been cooking, and where?"
      - "ASK: how did the two of them come to be partners?"
      - "ASK: who runs which side day to day — kitchen, catering, front of house?"
      - "ASK: what does reopening the dining room actually mean to them, in their own words? One sentence in Terry's voice beats a paragraph in ours."
      - "ASK: one specific thing — a dish one of them is known for, a habit, something they always say. Specifics are what get shared; adjectives are not."
      - "NEEDED: a photo of the two of them, in the kitchen or at the door. It will out-perform the graphic. No photos exist yet and AI imagery is off the table."

  - group: "The date and the practical facts"
    items:
      - "Opening Monday, October 5th, 2026."
      - "Hours 6:00am to 2:00pm, Monday through Friday."
      - "417 S 6th St, Leavenworth, KS 66048."
      - "Phone (913) 547-9994."
      - "lvcafetogo.com and facebook.com/LVCafeToGo."
      - "It is an opening, not a grand opening — the menu is brand new and needs time to settle. The celebration comes later."

  - group: "The history"
    items:
      - "Opened October 2005 — twenty-one years this month, almost to the week."
      - "Started in the historic Abernathy Building, near the Centennial Bridge, as a weekday breakfast-and-lunch counter."
      - "Daily specials, sandwiches made to order, soups, salads, home-style plates."
      - "Moved locations several times around Leavenworth over the years."
      - "Eventually set the dining room aside and went catering-only — dinners, buffets, office lunches."
      - "For years, much of the kitchen's output went out as Meals on Wheels: prepared meals for seniors and neighbors across the Leavenworth area. That work ends this fall."
      - "October 5th is the return to a dining room. Do NOT say we are back in the Abernathy Building — that is where it started, not where it is."

  - group: "The food"
    items:
      - "Breakfast: biscuits and gravy full or half, the Big Breakfast, burritos, 2/3 egg omelets, breakfast sandwiches. Burritos and omelets are build-your-own."
      - "Lunch: wraps, sandwiches, burgers and chicken — Navajo burger, patty melt, Philly steak, Reuben, clubhouse. Salads full or half, soup of the day, sides."
      - "Breakfast runs about $5 to $11, lunch mostly $8 to $12."
      - "Catering is not going anywhere: sit-down dinners with china and linen, buffets, drop-off, appetizer and station service. Fifteen guest minimum, dietary accommodations on request."

  - group: "How to end it"
    items:
      - "Ask a question. A cold page lives on comments, and comments are reach."
      - "Best one: what do you want to see on the menu? The menu is genuinely still being written, so the answer changes something."
      - "Ask people to share it. For a reopening, that is the whole distribution plan."

  - group: "Do not say"
    items:
      - "Nothing about the Meals on Wheels contract, the bid, who won it, or per-meal pricing. Say the work ends this fall and leave it there."
      - "Not 'grand opening'."
      - "Nothing we have not checked. A wrong hour or a wrong price on a post that gets shared is the expensive kind of mistake."

# ── The caption ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The post is the image AND this. The image is the thing that stops a
# thumb in the feed, so it carries four facts and no more; everything
# that needs reading lives here, where Facebook lets it be read.
#
# Shown on /studio/downloads/ with a copy button, so it can be pasted
# from the same phone that just saved the PNG. One string per paragraph.
# Write & and — as literals; Nunjucks escapes these on output.
caption:
  - "Twenty-one years ago this month, The Café opened as a small breakfast-and-lunch counter in the Abernathy Building, down by the Centennial Bridge. Daily specials, sandwiches made to order, soup, and home-style plates for whoever came through the door."
  - "A lot has changed since. We moved a few times. Eventually we set the dining room aside and put everything into catering — dinners, buffets, office lunches — and for years now much of what has left this kitchen went out in Meals on Wheels trays to seniors and neighbors across Leavenworth. That work has meant more to us than we can put in a post, and it comes to an end this fall."
  - "So we are doing the thing we have been talking about for a long time. We are opening the doors again."
  - "Monday, October 5th. Breakfast from 6, lunch until 2, Monday through Friday, at 417 S 6th St. Biscuits and gravy, omelets built the way you want them, burgers, wraps, salads, and a soup of the day. Catering is not going anywhere — call us for that the same as always."
  - "We are calling it an opening, not a grand opening. A brand new menu takes a while to settle, and we would rather get it right than get it loud. Come sit down, be patient with us, and tell us what you think."
  - "417 S 6th St, Leavenworth · Mon–Fri, 6am–2pm · (913) 547-9994 · lvcafetogo.com"
  - "What are you hoping to see on the menu? Tell us below — we are still writing it."

