{# Four facts. That is the whole brief.

   This used to carry a specials card as well, which put five things on an
   artboard that gets scrolled past in about a second and rendered at ~500px
   on a phone. A feed image is a headline, not a page: it earns the tap, and
   the caption does the talking. Specials, when there are some, go in the
   caption where they can be edited after posting — a typo in a PNG means a
   re-upload and a lost post. #}
<div class="canvas post">

    <header class="post-head">
        {# .wordmark--hero, not the print weight: this sits on a dark
           composited ground at screen size, which is the hero's situation
           exactly. See the wordmark section of piece.css. #}
        <div class="wordmark wordmark--light wordmark--hero post-wordmark">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>

        {#- The names, directly under the wordmark, in the accent red — on a
            cream plaque, and the plaque is not decoration.

            Red on teal is 1.3:1, the one pairing this palette forbids
            outright, and the lighter --coral only reaches 2.15:1 against the
            ground here — still under the 3:1 that large text needs. Red on
            cream is 5.08:1 and passes AA. So the red goes where it can be
            read, and the light plaque on a dark ground pulls the eye harder
            than any change of hue would have anyway. -#}
        <div class="post-names">
            <p class="p-display post-names-line">
                {%- for owner in site.owners %}{{ owner.name }}{% if not loop.last %} <span class="amp">&amp;</span> {% endif %}{% endfor -%}
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="post-filigree">
            {% include "partials/filigree.njk" %}
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="post-announce">
        <p class="p-display-italic post-kicker">Opening for Breakfast &amp; Lunch</p>
        <p class="p-display post-date">{{ site.opening.monthDay }}<sup>{{ site.opening.ordinal }}</sup></p>
    </section>

    {# When we are open. Ruled top and bottom rather than filled: a second
       cream card here would fight the names plaque, and the names win. #}
    <section class="post-facts">
        <p class="p-display post-days">{{ site.opening.hoursDays }}</p>
        <p class="p-display post-hours">
            {{ site.opening.opens.time }}<span class="ampm">{{ site.opening.opens.meridiem }}</span>
            &ndash;
            {{ site.opening.closes.time }}<span class="ampm">{{ site.opening.closes.meridiem }}</span>
        </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="post-foot">
        <p class="p-label post-catering">Email for Catering Options</p>
        <p class="p-body post-email">{{ site.email }}</p>
        {# The address is not on the brief, but a reopening post without one
           sends people to Google to find out where. Kept small and last. #}
        <p class="p-body post-addr">{{ site.address.street }} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </footer>

</div>
